// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1983790814" "Pirates of the Skies"
// DetailString :
"P1677433543" "You'd heard rumors that the Sky Raiders had upset someone big inside Arachnos, and a few questions had led you to Silver Mantis. The henchwoman, favorite assassin, and some say lover of Black Scorpion, she had a mission for a group of villains willing to crush the Sky Raiders for stepping over the line. <br><br>The first mission was easy enough. The Sky Raiders were desperate for any edge they could get. So desperate, in fact, that they were planning to steal the secrets of the Tsoo's tattoo magic. Silver Mantis sent you in to crush them and kidnap some Tsoo tattoo artists for the Mu Mystics of Arachnos to interrogate."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1583459904" "You'd heard rumors that the Sky Raiders had upset someone big inside Arachnos, and a few questions had led you to Silver Mantis. The henchwoman, favorite assassin, and some say lover of Black Scorpion, she had a mission for a group of villains willing to crush the Sky Raiders for stepping over the line. <br><br>The first mission was easy enough. The Sky Raiders were desperate for any edge they could get. So desperate, in fact, that they were planning to steal the secrets of the Tsoo's tattoo magic. Silver Mantis sent you in to crush them and kidnap some Tsoo tattoo artists for the Mu Mystics of Arachnos to interrogate. <br><br>The Sky Raider's next target was a hospital the Lost had put together in an unused office building. Seems they had some alien medicines from the Rikti War that the Raiders wanted. You stole the medicines from both sides, and dealt out a prescription for pain to anyone who crossed your path."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1306173742" "You'd heard rumors that the Sky Raiders had upset someone big inside Arachnos, and a few questions had led you to Silver Mantis. The henchwoman, favorite assassin, and some say lover of Black Scorpion, she had a mission for a group of villains willing to crush the Sky Raiders for stepping over the line. <br><br>The first mission was easy enough. The Sky Raiders were desperate for any edge they could get. So desperate, in fact, that they were planning to steal the secrets of the Tsoo's tattoo magic. Silver Mantis sent you in to crush them and kidnap some Tsoo tattoo artists for the Mu Mystics of Arachnos to interrogate. <br><br>The Sky Raider's next target was a hospital the Lost had put together in an unused office building. Seems they had some alien medicines from the Rikti War that the Raiders wanted. You stole the medicines from both sides, and dealt out a prescription for pain to anyone who crossed your path. <br><br>The Freakshow had set themselves up a little import/export business to bring cybernetics, weapons, and drugs over from the mainland. The Sky Raiders wanted to steal their shipments, Arachnos wanted them stopped, and Arachnos was also upset with the Freaks for keeping all of this secret and not paying Arachnos their cut. But Silver Mantis and Arachnos were the ones who'd hired you to make what they wanted to happen, happen. Too bad for Freaks and the Raiders."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission4Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P613498024" "You'd heard rumors that the Sky Raiders had upset someone big inside Arachnos, and a few questions had led you to Silver Mantis. The henchwoman, favorite assassin, and some say lover of Black Scorpion, she had a mission for a group of villains willing to crush the Sky Raiders for stepping over the line. <br><br>The first mission was easy enough. The Sky Raiders were desperate for any edge they could get. So desperate, in fact, that they were planning to steal the secrets of the Tsoo's tattoo magic. Silver Mantis sent you in to crush them and kidnap some Tsoo tattoo artists for the Mu Mystics of Arachnos to interrogate. <br><br>The Sky Raider's next target was a hospital the Lost had put together in an unused office building. Seems they had some alien medicines from the Rikti War that the Raiders wanted. You stole the medicines from both sides, and dealt out a prescription for pain to anyone who crossed your path. <br><br>The Freakshow had set themselves up a little import/export business to bring cybernetics, weapons, and drugs over from the mainland. The Sky Raiders wanted to steal their shipments, Arachnos wanted them stopped, and Arachnos was also upset with the Freaks for keeping all of this secret and not paying Arachnos their cut. But Silver Mantis and Arachnos were the ones who'd hired you to make what they wanted to happen, happen. Too bad for Freaks and the Raiders. <br><br>Silver Mantis's next mission sent you far off to Striga Island, where the Council was trying to sell some of their enhancement technology to the Sky Raiders. You snuck in through the vents and put a violent end to the negotiations and the negotiators."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission5Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3846014031" "You'd heard rumors that the Sky Raiders had upset someone big inside Arachnos, and a few questions had led you to Silver Mantis. The henchwoman, favorite assassin, and some say lover of Black Scorpion, she had a mission for a group of villains willing to crush the Sky Raiders for stepping over the line. <br><br>The first mission was easy enough. The Sky Raiders were desperate for any edge they could get. So desperate, in fact, that they were planning to steal the secrets of the Tsoo's tattoo magic. Silver Mantis sent you in to crush them and kidnap some Tsoo tattoo artists for the Mu Mystics of Arachnos to interrogate. <br><br>The Sky Raider's next target was a hospital the Lost had put together in an unused office building. Seems they had some alien medicines from the Rikti War that the Raiders wanted. You stole the medicines from both sides, and dealt out a prescription for pain to anyone who crossed your path. <br><br>The Freakshow had set themselves up a little import/export business to bring cybernetics, weapons, and drugs over from the mainland. The Sky Raiders wanted to steal their shipments, Arachnos wanted them stopped, and Arachnos was also upset with the Freaks for keeping all of this secret and not paying Arachnos their cut. But Silver Mantis and Arachnos were the ones who'd hired you to make what they wanted to happen, happen. Too bad for Freaks and the Raiders. <br><br>Silver Mantis's next mission sent you far off to Striga Island, where the Council was trying to sell some of their enhancement technology to the Sky Raiders. You snuck in through the vents and put a violent end to the negotiations and the negotiators. <br><br>The Sky Raiders' next target was a Crey Lab, hidden beneath an office building. Mantis ordered you to stop them, and to bring back information on what Crey was up to. It turns out that Crey was hard at work developing cloned synthetic super-humans, technology and techniques that the Sky Raiders were eager to steal. You cleaned the place out, stopping the Raiders and leaving no one at Crey to say who might have learned what."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PiratesOfTheSkiesSouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1384139841" "Duray's Beret"
// tDetailString :
"P2221227609" "You fished this military beret out of the sea after your battle with Colonel Duray, the leader of the Sky Raiders. It's only fitting you have a trophy, after you fought the Colonel and his <br><br>Pirates of the Skies <br><br>You'd heard rumors that the Sky Raiders had upset someone big inside Arachnos, and a few questions had led you to Silver Mantis. The henchwoman, favorite assassin, and some say lover of Black Scorpion, she had a mission for a group of villains willing to crush the Sky Raiders for stepping over the line. <br><br>The first mission was easy enough. The Sky Raiders were desperate for any edge they could get. So desperate, in fact, that they were planning to steal the secrets of the Tsoo's tattoo magic. Silver Mantis sent you in to crush them and kidnap some Tsoo tattoo artists for the Mu Mystics of Arachnos to interrogate. <br><br>The Sky Raider's next target was a hospital the Lost had put together in an unused office building. Seems they had some alien medicines from the Rikti War that the Raiders wanted. You stole the medicines from both sides, and dealt out a prescription for pain to anyone who crossed your path. <br><br>The Freakshow had set themselves up a little import/export business to bring cybernetics, weapons, and drugs over from the mainland. The Sky Raiders wanted to steal their shipments, Arachnos wanted them stopped, and Arachnos was also upset with the Freaks for keeping all of this secret and not paying Arachnos their cut. But Silver Mantis and Arachnos were the ones who'd hired you to make what they wanted to happen, happen. Too bad for Freaks and the Raiders. <br><br>Silver Mantis's next mission sent you far off to Striga Island, where the Council was trying to sell some of their enhancement technology to the Sky Raiders. You snuck in through the vents and put a violent end to the negotiations and the negotiators. <br><br>The Sky Raiders' next target was a Crey Lab, hidden beneath an office building. Mantis ordered you to stop them, and to bring back information on what Crey was up to. It turns out that Crey was hard at work developing cloned synthetic super-humans, technology and techniques that the Sky Raiders were eager to steal. You cleaned the place out, stopping the Raiders and leaving no one at Crey to say who might have learned what. Finally, it was time to bring it all down. You snuck aboard a container ship full of things stolen by the Sky Raiders. You fought your way out, and attacked the Sky Raider's floating off-shore base, setting it ablaze. Tired of your interference and all the damage you've cause, Colonel Duray himself joined the fight, determined to take you down. <br><br>The Sky Raiders' shot at the big-time is over for now. You've broken their dreams, and left their sea-base a sinking inferno. Silver Mantis was pleased with your work, and promised to send word along to Black Scorpion of your success. She also says that Arachnos fished Duray out of the sea, and have him in their custody now for questioning, but who knows how long that will last? The Rogue Isles have always been a haven for pirates, and you're pretty sure that the Pirates of the Skies will return once more."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2812350268" "Now that you're ready, let's cause some violence! Colonel Duray's first operation is also their biggest long-shot. Seems that they've noticed the tattoo magic of the Tsoo, and want to control it for themselves. Personally, I think just getting ink is for weaklings who don't have what it takes to drill some real metal into their bones, but those magic skin-scrawlings could give them some extra power. So you get to stop the Sky Raiders from getting it, and get to crack some Tsoo Heads in the meantime. That sounds like a great time out to me!"
// AcceptString :
"P2260482534" "Stop the Skyraiders from getting the secrets of Tsoo Tattoo magic."
// SendOffString :
"P3660633239" "You'll have 3 things to do in there. First, you have to defeat the leaders on both sides, and their personal guards. The Skyraiders have a Captain Lee, and the Tsoo have a Master Li. Don't worry about getting them confused, as long as they both end up the same way. Oh, and also find 2 of their tattoo artists, and return them to us. Scirocco is always interested in anything magic, having a few of these tattoo masters on ice could be a good bargaining chip."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P926010748" "Stop Skyraider attack"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1745249485" "You won't be done until you've crushed both Captain Lee and Master Li, and you've captured those tattoo artists."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1333383000" "The Skyraiders normally stick to high-technology thefts. They must be in trouble if they're experimenting with magic."

